standardClauses.text:
The Closing shall be subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the following conditions:

(a) The Company shall have adopted amended constitutional documents reflecting the rights of the Preferred Stock;

(b) The Company shall have obtained all necessary corporate approvals, including shareholder and board resolutions;

(c) The Investor shall have completed satisfactory due diligence;

(d) Each party shall have executed all transaction documents;

(e) The Company shall deliver to the Investor a duly executed share certificate (or evidence of book-entry registration) representing the Shares;

(f) No material adverse change shall have occurred in the Company's business, assets, or financial condition since the date of the most recent financial information provided to the Investor.

The Company represents and warrants to the Investor that, as of the Effective Date and the Closing Date:

(a) Organization: The Company is duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of its jurisdiction of incorporation;

(b) Authorization: The execution and delivery of this Agreement and the issuance of the Shares have been duly authorized by all necessary corporate action;

(c) Capitalization: The Company's capitalization is as set forth in Schedule B, and no shares are subject to preemptive rights, rights of first refusal, or similar rights not disclosed herein;

(d) Intellectual Property: The Company owns or has valid rights to all intellectual property material to its business;

(e) Litigation: There is no pending or threatened litigation that would materially affect the Company;

(f) Compliance: The Company is in material compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.

The Investor represents and warrants that: (i) the Investor has the authority and capacity to enter into this Agreement; (ii) the Investor is an accredited investor (or equivalent) as applicable; and (iii) the Shares are being acquired for investment purposes and not with a view to distribution.
